{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>The peder.</b> Many of the generation's sages explained it as the body, but what seems correct to me is that the peder was the fats. So too: 'and Aaron's sons the priests shall arrange the pieces' (Leviticus 1:8) — which are the pieces of the body — 'the head and the peder,' which are the fats, and there is omission of the letter vav, as is the way of the language: אדם פטדה וברקת, 'and he cut it into its pieces' and 'into the pieces of the body, its head and its peder' — or the meaning of 'the head' is together with the head, and similar to it are many [instances], and the trustworthy witness: 'and Moses caused to go up in smoke the head and the pieces and the peder' (Leviticus 8:20)." "<b>And they shall arrange.</b> Concerning the offspring of the herd, for it is large; and concerning the lamb, [it says] 'and arrange' (Leviticus 1:12)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Resolved הגוף as 'the body' rather than 'the hide'; Ibn Ezra disputes this common interpretation and instead identifies peder with fats. The three gemstone names אדם פטדה וברקת ( Exodus 28:17) are cited as a parallel for vav omission; left in Hebrew script as biblical Hebrew forms he quotes.", 1 "Reading בן הבקר literally as 'offspring of the herd,' i.e., the bovine animal, as opposed to the lamb in the next clause."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:08:27.944422066Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}